description:
Followup to bd:JMAP-6r7c.37. The .37 close added CustomCaTransport::from_pem_bytes for the most common operator-friction case (a single PEM file). The other two recommendations from .37 remain open:

1. **Multi-cert chains** — A private PKI typically has root + intermediate. CustomCaTransport stores one DER cert. A caller wanting to trust an intermediate has to construct their own TransportConfig impl from scratch.

2. **mTLS / client certs** — Mutual TLS requires the client to present a cert. CustomCaTransport only configures the trust root. A caller wanting mTLS rolls their own TransportConfig.

Proposed shape (from .37):

  pub struct CustomTransportBuilder {
      roots: Vec<Vec<u8>>,        // accept multiple DER roots
      client_certs: Option<Vec<u8>>,  // PEM bundle (chain)
      client_key: Option<Vec<u8>>,    // PEM-encoded PKCS8/PKCS1 private key
      timeouts: ...,
  }

  impl CustomTransportBuilder {
      pub fn new() -> Self;
      pub fn add_root_der(self, der: Vec<u8>) -> Self;
      pub fn add_root_pem(self, pem: &[u8]) -> Result<Self, ClientError>;
      pub fn add_roots_pem_bundle(self, pem_bundle: &[u8]) -> Result<Self, ClientError>;
      pub fn with_client_cert(self, cert_pem: Vec<u8>, key_pem: Vec<u8>) -> Self;
      pub fn build(self) -> impl TransportConfig;
  }

Implementation notes:
- reqwest::Certificate::from_pem_bundle already exists for the multi-cert PEM case.
- reqwest::Identity::from_pem (rustls feature) handles the client-cert + key pair.
- The 'rustls' feature is already enabled on reqwest in this workspace (see workspace TLS-stack policy).
- The existing CustomCaTransport stays for backward compat; new code uses CustomTransportBuilder.

Affects: crate-jmap-base-client/src/auth.rs.
Tests: extend tests/fixtures/tls/ with a chain fixture (root + intermediate) generated via openssl; mTLS test would need a client-cert fixture and a wiremock server configured to require a client cert (wiremock-rs may not support this; could use a static rustls server fixture).

Out of scope for bd:JMAP-6r7c.37 since the PEM-only convenience already lands the highest-frequency consumer benefit; the builder is a bigger API surface that should ride its own dedicated bead.
